package workflow

// BrowserUseInstructions is launch-only guidance for the machine browser
// setting. The daemon enforces these rules; the text never widens authority.
func BrowserUseInstructions() string {
	return `# Browser use through Clawdline

Browser preferences are configured in Settings → Chrome. Read ` + "`clawdline browser status`" + ` before choosing: it reports the ordered policy, independent automatic switches, profile readiness and this Session's choice. Try automatically enabled browsers in priority order. Native means your own browser tools, if actually available; Clawdline does not run them for you. Skip an unavailable browser only before executing an action. Never repeat a click, input or destructive action in another browser after execution or an uncertain result.
Use ` + "`clawdline browser`" + ` for test Chrome or the person's usual Chrome (open <url>, read, click <label> or --x/--y, type <text>, key <name>, scroll, viewport mobile|desktop, screenshot, close, release; ` + "`clawdline browser --help`" + `). A named ` + "`--browser isolated|user_chrome`" + ` normally obeys the automatic switch. Only when the person explicitly requests that browser may you add ` + "`--explicit`" + `: the choice applies to this Session, never changes global switches, and still requires a loaded extension and connected native host. Example: ` + "`clawdline browser open --browser isolated --explicit <url>`" + `. Never invent the person's explicit request.
Chrome profiles have separate tab numbers; always keep the selected mode with a tab. Every Clawdline action is recorded; the person may watch and take over from this machine or their phone. The person may also open a Session tab themselves; it starts under their control, so wait for handback before using it.
Use ` + "`close`" + ` to close a tab you own. ` + "`release`" + ` leaves it open. Never close or replace a tab the person is controlling. Prefer ` + "`read`" + ` and labels over coordinates.
` + "`browser_person_controlling`" + `: wait for handback, without looping. ` + "`browser_stopped`" + `: emergency stop; explicit requests never bypass it. ` + "`browser_session_busy`" + ` or ` + "`browser_tab_closing`" + `: wait for the existing result; never change browsers to replay it. ` + "`browser_setup_required`" + `: setup is incomplete or disconnected; preparing extension files alone is not installation. Ask the person to set that browser up from Settings → Chrome. Installing or connecting usual Chrome requires their separate permission. ` + "`browser_native_tools`" + ` means use your native tools when available, not that the daemon executed an action.
When a page needs the person (sign-in, CAPTCHA, payment or any confirmation with consequences), create a Clawdline note with kind "browser" asking them to take over the Chrome tab; its Take over button opens the live panel (` + "`clawdline guide note`" + `), and wait. Never ask for a password in chat; for a secret use a Secret Handoff and ` + "`clawdline secret run <note> -- clawdline browser type --stdin`" + `.
Do not buy, send messages, publish, delete or accept terms in the browser unless the person asked for that exact action.
This setting does not authorize installing software, changing the person's Chrome or spending money.`
}
